    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d969">

                <pb facs="0743" n="627" xml:id="pg627"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/13897, 13907.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Consul Canada to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-26T13:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 26, 1914, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Offices Constitutionalist Government being established in Vera Cruz. General
                    Aguilar called and congratulated me upon the orderly manner in which General
                    Funston evacuated and the clean condition in which he found the city. Generals
                    Carranza, Obregón and Alvarado announced to arrive this afternoon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canada</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
